window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>When a series of gruesome murders leaves a community in despair, a former local DJ decides to start a podcast and do something about it. But as his following grows, long-buried secrets from the past resurface revealing not everyone is who they truly seem....</p> <p><i>Radioman </i>explores themes of grief, trauma, deceit and family within a country at war with itself, questioning how much the past impacts the present and how betrayal, in its most extreme form, can rip a family to pieces. As one man journeys to catch a killer, will he survive the pressures to succeed or ultimately be consumed by his own downfall?</p> <p><b>Starring Nikolaj Coster-Waldau (</b><b><i>Game of Thrones</i></b><b>), David Morrissey (The Walking Dead), Divian Ladwa (Ant-Man), and Cathy Tyson (Mona Lisa). With audio production, sound design &amp; original music by Benbrick (Have You Heard George’s Podcast?). </b></p> <p><b>A Vespucci and Big Light Entertainment production for Audible Originals. </b> </p>"; 
